#3. A weather prediction system receives temperature and humidity measurements from two locations. The input matrix is X = [[30, 60], [35, 70]]. The model uses the weight matrix W = [[0.2, 0.5], [0.4, 0.3]]. Write a Python program to multiply the input matrix by the weight matrix and display the predicted output matrix for both locations.
import numpy as np

X = np.array([[30, 60],
              [35, 70]])

W = np.array([[0.2, 0.5],
              [0.4, 0.3]])

output = np.dot(X, W)

print("Predicted Output Matrix:\n", output)
